  "title": "Smile Makeover in Wellington, FL | Smiles By Jiveh",
  "metaDescription": "Planning a smile makeover in Wellington, FL? Smiles By Jiveh is a private, fee for service practice in Royal Palm Beach, caring for one patient at a time.",
  "slug": "smile-makeover-wellington-fl",
  "body": "Smiles By Jiveh plans smile makeovers for patients from Wellington, FL at its office at 11989 Southern Blvd in Royal Palm Beach, FL. Smiles By Jiveh is private, fee for service and out of network with insurance. A smile makeover can combine more than one treatment, such as porcelain or no-prep veneers, KOR whitening, dental bonding, crowns and implants.\n\n## What is a smile makeover at Smiles By Jiveh?\n\nA smile makeover combines cosmetic and restorative treatments into one plan, rather than a single procedure. Read more about [smile makeovers at Smiles By Jiveh](https://smilesbyjiveh.com/smile-makeovers/).\n\nSmiles By Jiveh is Dr. Farokh Jiveh's practice. Its approach is artistry plus advanced dentistry. The practice offers cosmetic treatments such as veneers, whitening and bonding. It also offers restorative treatments such as crowns, bridges and implants. You can [meet Dr. Jiveh](https://smilesbyjiveh.com/meet-dr-jiveh/) on our website.\n\nFor Wellington patients, Smiles By Jiveh offers both the cosmetic and the restorative treatments listed below.\n\n## Which treatments can a smile makeover include?\n\nSmiles By Jiveh offers the services below. A smile makeover can combine more than one of them, but it does not have to include all of them. Which ones fit depends on your teeth and your goals.\n\n- Veneers: [porcelain and no-prep veneers](https://smilesbyjiveh.com/dental-veneers/), thin coverings for the front of the teeth that change their shape, size or shade\n- Whitening: [KOR teeth whitening](https://smilesbyjiveh.com/teeth-whitening-treatment/), a teeth whitening treatment\n- Dental bonding: tooth colored material shaped onto a tooth\n- Tooth colored fillings: fillings that match the color of your teeth\n- Dental crowns and bridges: crowns cover a damaged tooth, and bridges replace missing teeth\n- Dental implants and implant-supported dentures: ways to replace missing teeth\n\nNearby teeth can drift into a gap over time and the bite can change, but it is not certain. Cleveland Clinic advises replacing missing teeth as soon as possible ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental bridges](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10921-dental-bridges)).\n\n## Is my oral health ready for cosmetic treatment?\n\nSmiles By Jiveh offers dental exams, digital x-rays and gum care alongside its cosmetic and restorative treatments.\n\nIf your plan includes an implant or a bridge, gum disease needs treating first. Reasons for caution before implant surgery include smoking or vaping, diabetes that is not well controlled, untreated gum disease, bone disorders, and some autoimmune conditions and their medicines ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental implants](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10903-dental-implants)).\n\nSome bone medicines (such as bisphosphonates and denosumab) carry a risk of jaw osteonecrosis, so implant surgery needs careful planning for people who take them ([AAOMS position paper, 2022](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35300956/)).\n\n## What upkeep does a smile makeover need?\n\nEach treatment in a makeover has its own care and its own trade-offs.\n\n- Bridges: Shaping a tooth for a bridge crown cannot be undone. Cleaning under a bridge every day matters, with a floss threader or a small interdental brush ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental bridges](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10921-dental-bridges)).\n- Bone around implants: An implant stimulates and helps protect the bone that remains around it, but it cannot rebuild bone that is already lost ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental implants](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10903-dental-implants)).\n- Gums around implants: Caught early, gum inflammation around an implant can often improve with a professional cleaning and better cleaning at home, though it can take weeks. Bone loss around an implant is harder to treat ([Heitz-Mayfield and Salvi 2018](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29926954/)).\n\n## Is Smiles By Jiveh fee for service?\n\nYes. Smiles By Jiveh is private, fee for service and out of network with insurance.\n\nThis applies to every treatment in a smile makeover, for patients from Wellington and Royal Palm Beach alike. You can read [how fee for service dentistry works](https://smilesbyjiveh.com/insurance-payment-options/) before you visit.\n\n## Visiting our Royal Palm Beach office from Wellington\n\nThe office is at 11989 Southern Blvd in Royal Palm Beach, FL, and welcomes patients from Wellington, FL.\n\nThe practice is closed Saturdays.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Is a smile makeover worth it?\n\nWhether a smile makeover is worth it depends on your goals, your oral health and the treatments your plan includes. Each treatment has its own care and trade-offs. For example, shaping a tooth for a bridge crown cannot be undone ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental bridges](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10921-dental-bridges)). An implant cannot rebuild bone that is already lost ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental implants](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10903-dental-implants)). Results vary.\n\n### What treatments are included in my smile makeover?\n\nA smile makeover can combine more than one cosmetic or restorative treatment. Smiles By Jiveh offers porcelain and no-prep veneers, KOR whitening, dental bonding, tooth colored fillings, crowns, bridges, implants and implant-supported dentures. Which of them a plan includes depends on your teeth and your goals.\n\n### What are the risks of a smile makeover?\n\nThe risks of a smile makeover depend on which treatments are included. Shaping a tooth for a bridge crown cannot be undone ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental bridges](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10921-dental-bridges)). About 4 in 10 people with implants have gum inflammation around one (peri-implant mucositis), and about 1 in 5 have bone loss from it (peri-implantitis). Case definitions varied between studies ([Derks and Tomasi 2015](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25495683/)). Gum disease needs treating first for an implant or a bridge ([Cleveland Clinic: Dental implants](https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/10903-dental-implants)).\n\n### Do you accept dental insurance?\n\nSmiles By Jiveh is private, fee for service and out of network with insurance. You can read how fee for service dentistry works for more.\n\n### Can a smile makeover include veneers?\n\nYes. Porcelain veneers and no-prep veneers are among the treatments Smiles By Jiveh offers, and a smile makeover can combine them with other treatments.\n\n### Can a smile makeover include dental implants?\n\nYes, a smile makeover can combine implants with other treatments. Smiles By Jiveh offers implants, implant-supported dentures, crowns and bridges as well as veneers, KOR whitening and bonding.\n\nIf you are in Wellington, FL and looking for A Different Kind of Dental Experience, [Book your smile makeover consultation](https://smilesbyjiveh.com/appointment/)."
